      "costUsd": 0.021395499999999998,
      "pronunciationText": "This is a practice video. The questions mix the differentiation rules, and none of them tells you which rule to use. Here's the first. A skate bowl's side follows the curve y equals x squared, minus six times the natural log of x. A skateboard rests flat against it where the slope is four. Find the equation of the line along the board. If you differentiate and set the gradient equal to four, you get two x-values, three and minus one. But there's no bowl at all at x equals minus one. So how do you pick the rule for an unseen question, and how do you know which answers to keep?"
    },
    {
