      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 0,
      "outputTokens": 0,
      "costUsd": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "Next, the domain. Before you differentiate, write down which x-values the function allows. A log needs its inside to be positive. A fraction needs its bottom to be nonzero. And tan has to stay away from its asymptotes. Why does this matter? An x-value outside the domain has no point on the curve, so there's no tangent there either, even if the algebra produces it. So the domain picks which answers you keep."
    },
