      "inputTokens": 405,
      "outputTokens": 2847,
      "costUsd": 0.0258255,
      "pronunciationText": "Back to the first question. The function is x squared minus six natural log x, so the last step is a subtraction. That means you differentiate each term on its own. The derivative is two x, minus six over x. The domain is x greater than zero, because the natural log needs a positive input. Write that beside the working now, before you solve anything."
