      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 0,
      "outputTokens": 0,
      "costUsd": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "The tangent has gradient four, so set two x minus six over x equal to four. Multiply through by x, and you get x squared minus two x minus three equals zero. That factorises to x minus three, times x plus one, so x is three or minus one. Now check the domain. Minus one isn't greater than zero, so reject it. At x equals three, the height of the curve is nine minus six natural log three. So the tangent is y minus that height equals four, times x minus three. Tidy it up, and the tangent is y equals four x, minus three, minus six natural log three."
    },
