      "outputTokens": 739,
      "costUsd": 0.006697,
      "pronunciationText": "By the chain rule, the derivative is two x over x squared minus four. The domain needs x squared minus four positive, so x is below minus two or above two. Setting the derivative to one gives x squared minus two x minus four equals zero, so x is one plus or minus root five. One minus root five is about minus one point two four, outside the domain. So x equals one plus root five. Keeping both is the mistake."
