      "costUsd": 0.012348,
      "pronunciationText": "Zero, one isn't on the curve, so name the touching point x equals a, with a positive. The tangent is y minus natural log ay equals one over a, times x minus a. Put in zero, one: one minus natural log ay equals minus one, so natural log ay is two, and ay is e squared. The tangent is y equals x over e squared, plus one. The gradient at x equals zero can't work, because zero isn't in the domain."
